# 4 Carat Marquise Diamond Price ({{year}}): 3 Reasons Lab Beats Natural

![Three loose 4 carat marquise diamonds held in jeweller tweezers against a soft grey backdrop as the DiamondCritics featured image for the {{year}} 4 carat marquise diamond price guide titled 3 reasons lab beats natural](/images/4-carat-marquise-diamond-price.jpg "4 Carat Marquise Diamond Price 3 Reasons Lab Beats Natural")

## TL;DR — 4 Carat Marquise Diamond Price in One Scroll

**4 carat marquise diamond price** starts at **[$5,027](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27304493?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** for IGI E-VVS2 lab-grown. Natural starts at **[$118,910](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28541553?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** for GIA 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal. Natural ceiling is **$193,183** for 4.17ct D-IF Ideal. The gap is **$113,883** for a stone that reads the same on the hand.

**The 3 reasons lab beats natural at 4ct (all 3 covered in full below):**

- **Reason 1 — The $113,883 price gap buys a 23x premium for the same face-up.** Lab 4ct and natural 4ct both measure 16.0 × 8.0 mm. On the hand, nobody can tell them apart.
- **Reason 2 — Natural inventory collapses to 3 stones.** Current certified market scan shows 3 natural 4ct marquise stones in stock. Lab shows 7 — all E-VVS2 Ideal or Excellent cut. Selection is dead on natural.
- **Reason 3 — Every lab 4ct is top-grade E-VVS2.** Lab inventory at this tier skips mid-grade entirely. You get near-colourless + near-flawless at the floor price. Natural at the floor is D-VS2 — one clarity grade lower than every lab stone.

→ Our pick lab: **[IGI 4.0ct E-VVS2 Ideal at $5,027](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30163254?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — floor price + Ideal cut + near-flawless clarity.
→ Our pick natural: **[GIA 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal at $118,910](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28541553?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — natural floor + D colour + Ideal cut.

**Priority:** at 4ct, lab is the honest answer for every buyer who does not care about resale. The $113,883 difference buys a house down payment, three years of mortgage, or a Tesla with change. Pick lab. Spend the saving on a platinum V-tip setting and the honeymoon.

## Expert Summary

4 carat marquise diamond price sits in a $5,027–$193,183 band in current certified market inventory. The lab floor is $5,027 for IGI 4.0ct E-VVS2. The natural floor is $118,910 for GIA 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal. The ceiling is $193,183 for GIA 4.17ct D-IF Ideal. Face-up size is 16.0 × 8.0 mm at 2.00 length-to-width ratio — reads bigger than a 4ct round on the finger.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/)-certified diamond expert. 4ct marquise is the tier where the lab arbitrage window stops being arguable. It is $113,883 wide — enough to buy a car, remodel a kitchen, or clear a mortgage year. The three stones in natural 4ct inventory give you no selection flexibility. The seven stones in lab inventory are all top-grade E-VVS2. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every carat tier from 0.5 through 5ct.

This guide covers the full certified market audit at 4ct marquise natural (3 stones) and lab (7 stones), the 3 reasons lab beats natural at this tier, the 3-Stone Natural Trap, the $113,883 Lab Arbitrage Window, the 16mm Statement Scale, and the setting math from $12k lab to $220k natural. All prices verified against live certified inventory. Pricing presented as independent market research.

## 4 Carat Marquise Diamond Price — The Market Floor

The absolute cheapest certified 4ct marquise in current market inventory is **$5,027** for IGI E-VVS2 lab-grown. The natural floor is **$118,910** for GIA 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal — a 23.6x premium for a stone that reads the same on the finger.

