**Verdict:** The natural floor is Ideal cut D-VS2 — a strong configuration. The lab floor is Excellent cut E-VVS2 at 4% of the price. For the extra $113,883, natural gives you one colour grade and the "mined" label. Lab gives you back two clarity grades and the saving. At 4ct, the maths is one-sided.

## 3 Reasons Lab Beats Natural at 4 Carats

**The 3 reasons below are the whole lab-vs-natural case at 4ct marquise.** Each one stands alone. Stacked together, they turn the choice from "worth considering" to "obvious." If you came here looking for an excuse to pick natural, I will give you one honest one at the end. For every other buyer, lab wins.

### Reason 1 — The $113,883 Price Gap at Identical Face-Up

4ct marquise natural starts at **[$118,910](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28541553?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**. 4ct marquise lab starts at **[$5,027](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27304493?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**. The gap is $113,883. Both stones measure 16.0 × 8.0 mm. On the finger, nobody tells them apart. Not your mother, not your jeweller, not a GIA grader without the certificate in hand.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Spec</th><th>Natural 4ct Floor</th><th>Lab 4ct Floor</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Price</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28541553?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$118,910</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27304493?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$5,027</a></td><td>Lab is 4% of natural. 23.6x price multiplier for the same look.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Face-up (mm)</strong></td><td>16.0 × 8.0</td><td>16.0 × 8.0</td><td>Identical. The eye cannot tell them apart.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>What $113,883 also buys</strong></td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>House down payment, 3 years of mortgage, a Tesla Model Y with change.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Resale realistic (lab)</strong></td><td>$55k+ natural</td><td>$500–$700 lab</td><td>Natural resale wins. But $113k spent now vs $55k back in 10 years = $58k lost either way.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The gap is the single biggest absolute-dollar arbitrage window on the whole marquise price chart. Even with natural's resale advantage, you lose less picking lab. The maths does not flip until the natural stone appreciates 100%+ — rare on fancy shapes at this size.

