### Reason 3 — Every Lab 4ct Is Top-Grade E-VVS2

All 7 lab 4ct stones in current inventory are **E colour, VVS2 clarity**. Six are 4.0ct exact weight. One is 4.0ct at $5,080. The grade distribution does not spread — every stone is near-colourless + near-flawless. On natural, the floor stone is D-VS2 — one clarity grade worse than every lab stone in the market.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Spec</th><th>Natural Floor (D-VS2)</th><th>Lab Floor (E-VVS2)</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Colour</strong></td><td>D (colourless)</td><td>E (colourless)</td><td>Natural wins by one grade. Visually identical face-up.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Clarity</strong></td><td>VS2</td><td>VVS2</td><td>Lab wins by one grade. VVS2 is cleaner to the loupe.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cut</strong></td><td>Ideal</td><td>Excellent or Ideal</td><td>Both top-tier. 4 of 7 lab stones are Ideal.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Price per stone</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28541553?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$118,910</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30163254?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$5,027</a></td><td>The one-grade colour trade saves you $113,883.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The one colour grade from D to E is worth exactly nothing face-up at 4ct marquise. The one clarity grade from VS2 to VVS2 is worth more to the eye — VVS2 reads cleaner through the open belly of the stone (see the official [GIA clarity scale](https://4cs.gia.edu/en-us/diamond-clarity/) for grade boundaries). Lab wins the quality comparison and the price comparison in the same stroke.

## The 3-Stone Natural Trap at 4 Carats

**The 3-Stone Natural Trap is the moment you realise natural 4ct marquise is not a market — it is a shortlist.** Three stones. Three. You get what the suppliers happen to have cut this quarter. If your partner wants a specific carat weight (say 4.25ct), you wait months. If a colour grade matters (D only), you have one option at $118,910. If an IF or FL cert matters, you have one option at $193,183.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Buyer want</th><th>Natural 4ct options</th><th>Lab 4ct options</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>D colour</strong></td><td>2 stones (D-VS2, D-IF)</td><td>0 stones (all E)</td><td>Natural wins D. Lab buyers pick E or wait.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Exact 4.00ct weight</strong></td><td>0 stones</td><td>7 stones</td><td>Lab wins exact-weight. Natural starts at 4.02ct.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Under $50,000</strong></td><td>0 stones</td><td>7 stones</td><td>Lab wins any realistic 4ct budget.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Over 4.5ct in this tier</strong></td><td>0 stones</td><td>0 stones</td><td>Both tiers top out at 4.21ct. Jump to 5ct for bigger.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>IGI vs GIA cert</strong></td><td>GIA only</td><td>IGI only</td><td>GIA matters more on natural. <a href="https://www.igi.org/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">IGI</a> is industry-standard for lab.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The 3-Stone Natural Trap means natural buyers at 4ct are not picking from a market — they are picking from a shortlist of three. Lab buyers get seven stones at a consistent spec and price. For every normal buyer, the trap is a reason to buy lab. For a buyer who needs the "mined D" story, it is a reason to pay $118,910.

