## The 4 Prong Rules Still Apply at 4 Carats

**The 4 Prong Rules from the [3ct marquise guide](/3-carat-marquise-diamond-price) scale with the stone.** At 4ct, tips extend 8.0 mm from the stone centre — a longer moment arm than 3ct. The chip risk is higher. The setting investment matters even more.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Why it matters at 4ct</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Rule 1 — V-tip prongs</strong></td><td>8mm tips need full-wrap protection</td><td>Non-negotiable at 4ct. Chip = $25k+ re-cut cost.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Rule 2 — Six prongs</strong></td><td>Shoulders 8mm from centre need shoulder support</td><td>Four-prong sets at 4ct are a mistake.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Rule 3 — Platinum</strong></td><td>Lab stone or $119k natural — the setting is insurance</td><td>Yellow or rose gold prongs fail at 4ct.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Rule 4 — Retighten every 2 years</strong></td><td>Platinum still drifts under daily wear</td><td>15-minute inspection prevents $25k loss.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** All 4 Prong Rules apply harder at 4ct than 3ct. The [Ten Prong Solitaire Platinum at $1,200](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-311240?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) satisfies all 4 rules under $1,500. Trying to buy 4ct natural with a cheap 4-prong gold setting is a $118,910 stone one bump from a chip.

