## Comparison — 4ct Marquise vs 3ct and 5ct Marquise

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Spec</th><th>3ct Marquise</th><th>4ct Marquise</th><th>5ct Marquise</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Face-up (mm)</strong></td><td>15.0 × 7.5</td><td>16.0 × 8.0</td><td>17.5 × 8.75</td><td>4ct is 6% bigger than 3ct, 15% smaller than 5ct.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Face-up area (mm²)</strong></td><td>88.4</td><td>100.5</td><td>120.3</td><td>4ct area jump from 3ct is 13%. Noticeable on finger.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Natural floor price</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28651376?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$54,687</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28541553?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$118,910</a></td><td>$177,964+</td><td>4ct natural is 2.2x 3ct natural for 13% more face-up.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Lab floor price</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30343375?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,819</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27304493?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$5,027</a></td><td>$5,480+</td><td>Lab price scales 32% from 3ct to 4ct. Natural scales 117%.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Stones in natural inventory</strong></td><td>14</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>4ct is the thinnest natural inventory tier.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Stones in lab inventory</strong></td><td>20+</td><td>7</td><td>30+</td><td>Lab inventory also narrows at 4ct — but still 2.3x natural.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reads as (face-up)</strong></td><td>3ct round</td><td>Larger than 4ct round</td><td>Larger than 5ct round</td><td>Marquise length advantage grows with carat.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** 4ct marquise is the "price-cliff tier" — natural jumps 117% from 3ct for only 13% more face-up. Lab barely moves. If your budget flexes to $120k, 3ct natural at $54,687 gets you 88% of the face-up for 46% of the price. If your budget sits at $5k, 4ct lab at $5,027 gets you 13% more size than 3ct lab for $1,208 more. On every honest axis, 4ct is a lab tier.

