## Pros and Cons of 4 Carat Marquise

**Pros:**

- **Biggest absolute lab-vs-natural arbitrage window on the marquise chart** ($113,883).
- **Every lab stone is top-grade** E-VVS2. No decision fatigue on specs.
- **Reads bigger than a 4ct round** by 25% face-up area. Length advantage peaks here.
- **Lab inventory stays under $5,080 ceiling** — the whole tier is one price.
- **Natural inventory is all Ideal cut.** Cut-quality concessions are zero.

**Cons:**

- **Natural inventory is 3 stones.** No selection flexibility.
- **Natural floor is $118,910.** Big budget line even for high-income buyers.
- **16mm length overwhelms petite fingers.** Size 4–5 need east-west mount or step down.
- **Setting cost is $8k–$18k minimum.** All 4 Prong Rules are mandatory, not optional.
- **Natural resale realistic at $55k+** but 10-year horizon locks in opportunity cost.

### How to Beat the Cons

The 3-stone natural inventory solves by picking lab. The petite finger issue solves with east-west mounting or a step down to 3ct. The setting cost solves by budgeting the Prong Rules investment from day one as part of the stone decision. The resale lock-in solves by picking lab — $5,027 is a rounding error in a wedding budget.

## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a 4 carat marquise diamond cost?

A 4 carat marquise diamond cost starts at **$5,027** for IGI E-VVS2 lab-grown. Natural starts at **$118,910** for GIA 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal. Ceiling for natural is **$193,183** for 4.17ct D-IF Ideal. Ceiling for lab is **$5,080**. The gap is the biggest on any marquise carat tier.

### Why does 4 carat marquise lab beat natural?

**The 3 reasons:**
1. The $113,883 price gap buys a 23.6x premium for the same face-up size.
2. Natural inventory collapses to 3 stones — lab has 7, all E-VVS2.
3. Every lab 4ct stone is near-flawless clarity VVS2 — one grade better than the natural floor.

On a 16mm × 8mm face-up stone, no observer tells lab from natural without the certificate.

### Is lab or natural better at 4 carat marquise?

**Lab wins objective value by 23.6x at 4ct.** $5,027 lab vs $118,910 natural for the same face-up size. Lab wins on clarity (VVS2 vs VS2). Natural wins on colour by one grade (D vs E). Natural wins resale (45–55% of retail at this tier) — but the absolute dollar loss is still less with lab.

### What is the cheapest 4 carat marquise diamond?

The cheapest certified 4 carat marquise is **[$5,027 IGI 4.0ct E-VVS2 Ideal Cut lab-grown](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30163254?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**. The cheapest natural is **[$118,910 GIA 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28541553?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — 23.6x the lab floor.

### Why does a 4 carat marquise need V-tip prongs?

At 4ct, marquise tips extend 8.0 mm from the stone centre. Standard round prongs leave tips exposed. The chip risk from a single bump is high. V-tip prongs wrap around each point from both sides. Chip risk reduction: 60–70%. Cost premium: $600–$1,000. At 4ct the rule is not optional.

### What setting is best for 4 carat marquise?

**Platinum V-tip six-prong setting** satisfies all 4 Prong Rules. Pair with a pavé halo for added perceived width or three-stone with trapezoid flankers for added depth. Total setting cost: $8,000–$18,000+ depending on halo detail. See [marquise halo engagement ring](/marquise-halo-engagement-ring) guide.

### Does a 4 carat marquise look as big as a 4 carat round?

**Bigger.** A 4ct marquise is 100.5 mm² face-up vs 80.1 mm² for a 4ct round — marquise wins area by 25%. The length advantage is 59% (16.0 mm marquise vs 10.1 mm round). The one trade-off is width — marquise 8mm vs round 10.1mm, so side-to-side coverage lags.

### What clarity should I buy at 4 carat marquise?

**VS2 is the clarity floor on natural, VVS2 on lab.** All current natural 4ct inventory is VS2 or better. All lab inventory is VVS2 or better. On a 16mm × 8mm face-up stone, VS2 is still eye-clean when well-cut. Jumping to IF or FL on natural adds $75,000+ for loupe- or microscope-only distinctions.

### What color grade is best for 4 carat marquise?

**D on natural, E on lab.** The 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal at $118,910 is the natural floor and our top pick — D colour comes free at this tier. On lab, E colour at the floor is near-colourless and reads identical to D face-up.

### How often do I need to retighten the prongs on a 4 carat marquise?

**Every 2 years minimum.** At 4ct the stone value and the 8mm tip length both raise the stakes. A 15-minute jeweller inspection catches drift before stone loss. Most retailers that sold the ring include free retightening for life.

### Can I resell a 4 carat marquise diamond?

Resale at 4ct natural marquise returns **45–55% of retail** — strong by fancy-shape standards because 4ct crosses the "investment-grade" line. Lab resale returns 8–12%. For resale-focused buyers, natural GIA at 4ct is defensible. For everyone else, lab is the honest answer.

### What is the price per carat for 4 carat marquise?

At 4ct natural, price per carat runs **$29,588 to $46,331/ct** ($118,910–$193,183 divided by 4). Lab per-carat sits at **$1,257 to $1,270/ct** ($5,027–$5,080 divided by 4). Natural per-carat at 4ct is the highest on the marquise chart because of the "statement tier" premium combined with thin inventory.

### What length-to-width ratio is best for 4 carat marquise?

**1.95 to 2.05** is the sweet spot at 4ct. The classic 2.00 L:W gives 16.0 × 8.0 mm — the standard measurements. If the length overwhelms a petite finger, drop to 1.90 L:W for a shorter silhouette (15.6 × 8.2 mm). Full logic in our [marquise L:W ratio guide](/marquise-diamond-length-to-width-ratio).

### Is 4ct marquise worth it vs 3ct?

**On lab, yes — $1,208 for 13% more face-up area.** Easy stretch. On natural, no — $64,223 premium for 13% more face-up is the worst per-dollar scale on the marquise chart. If budget flexes to $120k, 3ct natural is the smarter buy. 4ct natural is only for buyers who want the "4 carat" number specifically.

### How many 4 carat marquise diamonds are in the certified market right now?

**3 natural stones and 7 lab stones** at the time of this guide. The 3 natural are the GIA 4.02ct D-VS2 Ideal at $118,910, the GIA 4.21ct F-VS1 Ideal at $134,383, and the GIA 4.17ct D-IF Ideal at $193,183. All 7 lab are IGI E-VVS2 at $5,027 or $5,080.

> **"After 15 years grading diamonds, the hardest conversation I have is with a buyer who already decided they want natural 4ct marquise before they saw the lab price. The $113,883 saving is not an abstract number. It is a down payment on a house. It is three years of mortgage. For my own ring, I would pick the lab E-VVS2 at $5,027 every single time and spend the saved money on life."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

