## Why 4ct Lab Marquise Beats 4ct Round Lab on Size Per Dollar

A 4ct round lab diamond measures 10.1 mm across — face-up area of 80.1 mm². A 4ct marquise lab measures 16.0 × 8.0 mm — face-up area of 100.5 mm². The marquise beats the round on area by 25%, on length by 59%, and on starting lab price by 10% ($5,027 vs typical $5,600).

For buyers who want the biggest-looking lab stone per dollar at the 4ct tier, marquise is the clear winner on face-up measurements. The trade-off is the width — a 4ct marquise is 8.0 mm wide vs 10.1 mm for the round. Side-to-side finger coverage lags.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Spec</th><th>4ct Marquise Lab</th><th>4ct Round Lab</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Face-up (mm)</strong></td><td>16.0 × 8.0</td><td>10.1 Ø</td><td>Marquise is 59% longer than round diameter.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Face-up area (mm²)</strong></td><td>100.5</td><td>80.1</td><td>Marquise wins area by 25%.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Lab floor price</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30163254?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$5,027</a></td><td>~$5,600</td><td>Marquise is 10% cheaper than round at lab floor.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Reads as</strong></td><td>"Dramatic 4ct statement"</td><td>"Classic 4ct round"</td><td>Marquise reads bigger and more distinctive.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** For "biggest-looking lab ring per dollar" at the 4ct tier, marquise beats round on every measure that matters. Pay less, get 25% more face-up area, get the more distinctive silhouette. The width trade-off matters only if side-to-side coverage is a priority. Full comparison in our [round diamond vs marquise](/round-diamond-vs-marquise) guide.

## How to Verify a 4 Carat Marquise Before You Buy

Three checks every stone must pass before you add to cart.

**Check 1 — The certificate measurements.** For a 4ct marquise at 2.00 L:W, measurements should read close to 16.0 × 8.0 × 5.0 mm. If length is below 15.5 mm, the stone is cut deep and wasting carat weight below the girdle. More in our [marquise ideal proportions guide](/marquise-cut-diamond-ideal-proportions).

**Check 2 — The HD video for bow-tie severity.** The bow-tie risk is highest at 4ct because the stone belly is at its biggest. Open the 360° video. Faint diagonal shading = accept. Hard dark band = reject. See [marquise diamond bow-tie](/marquise-diamond-bow-tie).

**Check 3 — Confirm the setting supports V-tip six-prong platinum.** Before committing to the stone, confirm the setting you want satisfies all 4 Prong Rules. Standard round-prong 14k gold settings fail the check. Specify platinum V-tip six-prong from the start.

I run these three checks on every 4ct marquise before I quote a client. The stone has to pass the first two. The setting is the third — and often the difference between a ring that lasts 50 years intact and one that comes back with a chipped tip after 18 months.

